  "description": "OPAKUO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H92 Co8 Dy2 N10 O30,C2 H3 N1,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co7 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co8 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.894-3.768 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.96-107.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy2Co8(μ3-OCH3)2(L)4(HL)2(OAc)2(NO3)2(CH3CN)2]·CH3CN·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
